      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "Now to get started with NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 9.56,
          "en": "we'll start with a very basic, simple dummy Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 10.17,
          "end": 12.27,
          "en": "We'll start with an app that has a counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.27,
          "end": 15.15,
          "en": "that can be incremented and decremented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 17.94,
          "en": "And of course, I really wanna say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.94,
          "end": 20.22,
          "en": "and emphasize this right away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.22,
          "end": 24.93,
          "en": "this is not an app where you would need NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.93,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "Instead using NgRx for an app like this would be overkill.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 32.67,
          "en": "You would be doing a lot of unnecessary setup work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.67,
          "end": 35.91,
          "en": "that would not really be worth the effort.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.91,
          "end": 39.39,
          "en": "But I'm deliberately using a very simple app like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.39,
          "end": 42.9,
          "en": "which is split up across two components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.9,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "for outputting and controlling the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 50.51,
          "en": "and a service to slowly introduce NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 53.25,
          "en": "and all its core concepts step by step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.25,
          "end": 56.1,
          "en": "so that you could then use NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.1,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "in more complex apps thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "But for learning it, starting with a complex app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 64.38,
          "en": "would probably not be ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "Therefore, attached to this lecture here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 70.35,
          "en": "you find this starting project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "and you actually find it in two versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 77.19,
          "en": "One version that uses Ng modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.19,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "and also a standalone version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "where we're using Standalone Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "Using NgRx, as you will see, will be quite similar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 89.25,
          "en": "no matter which approach you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.25,
          "end": 91.56,
          "en": "And you will learn about both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.56,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "in the next lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 95.34,
          "en": "and you can therefore then simply follow along",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.34,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "with the approach you wanna use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 100.47,
          "en": "or the approach you have to use in the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.47,
          "end": 103.22999999999999,
          "en": "you might be working on in your job.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.22999999999999,
          "end": 106.56,
          "en": "So you'll find these two starting projects attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.56,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "and it's exactly the same app using the same two Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 115.49000000000001,
          "en": "and this one service just with or without Ng modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.21000000000001,
          "end": 120.27,
          "en": "So now that we get this starting project here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.27,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "and we get this big picture earlier in this section here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 129.42,
          "en": "it is now time to get started with NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 129.42,
          "end": 131.73,
          "en": "And for that in your Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.73,
          "end": 135.06,
          "en": "no matter if it's using Standalone Components or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.06,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "you can install NgRx by opening your terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 139.98,
          "en": "your system terminal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.98,
          "end": 143.16,
          "en": "And here I'm using the one integrated into my IDE,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 143.16,
          "end": 145.92000000000002,
          "en": "which in this case is Visual Studio Code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.92000000000002,
          "end": 147.96,
          "en": "But you can of course also manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.96,
          "end": 151.26,
          "en": "navigate into your project folder in your terminal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 151.26,
          "end": 152.433,
          "en": "or command prompt.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.27,
          "end": 155.73,
          "en": "And then once you are in your project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.73,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "in that terminal or command prompt,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 160.02,
          "en": "you can run ng add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.02,
          "end": 162.36,
          "en": "which is using the Angular CLI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.36,
          "end": 165.21,
          "en": "for adding a library to your project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 165.21,
          "end": 168.903,
          "en": "And then @ngrx/store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 175.86,
          "en": "And this must be written exactly like this @ngrx/store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.79,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "And it's always the same command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 181.923,
          "en": "no matter if you are using Standalone Components or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.76,
          "end": 187.76,
          "en": "And what this will do is it will download and install NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.29,
          "en": "so this third party library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
